  "id": "scene-001",
  "title": "Web Architecture with Load Balancer, App Servers, Cache, and Database",
  "question": "Explain a web architecture where clients reach a load balancer, which branches to three application servers. Every server can read a shared cache and a shared database; the cache can miss and fall back to the database. Show the separate request, cache-hit, cache-miss and response paths clearly.",
  "summary": "Clients contact a load balancer that distributes requests to three identical application servers. Each server first checks a shared in‑memory cache; on a hit it returns data directly, on a miss it queries the shared database and then populates the cache before responding.",
  "diagramType": "system",
  "visualStrategy": "Progressive construction of 5 core objects (load balancer, three app servers, shared cache, shared database) with clear connection arrows for request, cache‑hit, cache‑miss, and response flows.",
